namespace Rasa.Services.Preloader
{
    /// <summary>
    /// The named bosses the boss titles (BossTitles) ask for and nothing in the world spawned: 32 of them, without whom seven
    /// of the fourteen titles could not be earned (Abyss 8 of its 9 missing, Thunderhead 7 of 9, Crucible 5 of 6, Pools 3
    /// of 10, Plateau 1 of 5, Ashen Desert 1 of 6, Descent 7 of the 8 it needs 7 of). BossTitles counts a boss by the
    /// client's name for it (creature.name_id) on one of its battlefield's maps, so a creature row of that name standing
    /// on such a map is all a boss needs; BossTitles itself is not changed.
    ///
    /// Additive only: inserts of new rows (creature, creature_stat, creature_appearance, creature_action, spawnpool), ids
    /// <see cref="FirstCreatureId"/>.. for the creatures and their pools (a pool has its creature's id) and
    /// <see cref="FirstActionId"/>.. for the attack rows of their own. Down deletes exactly those. Nothing existing is
    /// updated. The ids are clear of upstream's: its creature, spawnpool and creature_action ids end below 650000.
    ///
    /// Where they come from (our own earlier work for these titles, re-checked against this world):
    ///  - 18 (Abyss, Thunderhead's Aramix, Arthox, Porthox and Irrogar, Pools, Descent's Snuffy, Y'mas and Billy Bob):
    ///    the boss rows made for the titles from the NPC workbook (TabulaRasa-NPC-Locations, tab "Boss spawns": the zone
    ///    band's level, health 100 x level + 500, armor 200 + 5 x level; attacks copied from a creature of the boss's
    ///    family and scaled to its level). The workbook names each boss and gives its place in words only; the spot was
    ///    chosen on the walkable ground in that bearing and distance from the place it names, 40 m or more from safe
    ///    ground and 70 m from AFS turrets, and kept only where the client's own floor is within 0.8 m of it.
    ///  - 14 (Descent's four Preceptors; Juroaz, Esoobac and the Warden Abomination on Thunderhead; Overseer Jirex;
    ///    Crucible's Preceptor Molitor, Archfiend Krubb, Coercer Mungrel, Defiler Sedge and Maxxum Ugoretz; Plateau's
    ///    Advanced Juggernaut Prototype): where the missions that name them stood them in our mission world, with the
    ///    same boss rule for health and armor at the level of the zone's other boss rows. Their attacks are the world's
    ///    own rows of their kind (the Thrax officers share the Thrax boss rows of upstream's boss pools 520013 and
    ///    520004), but for three that have rows of their own (Vaasti, Esoobac, the Juggernaut).
    /// The positions are our choice, not retail spawn points: the client's data names these bosses and their missions
    /// but holds no spawn point for any of them.
    ///
    /// Only retail entity classes. Every boss stands alone on an automatic point pool with the respawn upstream's boss
    /// pools have (BossSpawnpoolPreloader: respown_time 500, in tenths of a second).
    /// </summary>
    public static class TitleBossesSeed
    {
        public const uint FirstCreatureId = 9300001;
